						<main id="main-content" class="asic-page__main">
								<header class="asic-page__header">
									<!-- Page header component goes here -->						
									<h1 class="asic-text-title-large">
										Apply for auditor or authorised audit company registration
									</h1>
								</header>							

							<div class="asic-page__article">
								
								<!-- Prose component goes here -->								
<p class="intro">This page contains information on registering as an individual or authorised audit company.</p>
<h2>Before you start</h2>
<p>Before you apply, you need to:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="#rg" data-anchor="#rg">read our regulatory guidance</a></li>
<li><a href="#pf" data-anchor="#pf">read our Pro Forma conditions</a></li>
<li><a href="#fees" data-anchor="#fees">understand the fees and payment options</a></li>
</ul>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h3><a id="rg"></a>Regulatory guidance</h3>
<p>Read our Regulatory Guide 180:</p>
<p class="rg-link">Regulatory Guide 180 <em>Auditor registration </em>(<a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/regulatory-guides/rg-180-auditor-registration" title="RG 180 Auditor registration">RG 180</a>).</p>
<p>RG 180 includes the following sections which explain what information you will need to give ASIC for registration, what documentary proof you'll need to support your application and the application process. They also tell you about the conditions we may impose on your registration.</p>
<ul>
<li>Section B <em>Registering as a registered company auditor</em></li>
<li>Section C <em>Registering as an authorised audit company</em></li>
</ul>
<p>You can download Word versions of the documents listed in Appendix 1 of RG 180.</p>
<p>See <a href="#tips" data-anchor="#tips">Useful tips and application templates</a>.</p>
<h3><a id="pf"></a>Pro Forma conditions</h3>
<p>You should also download and read the relevant Pro Forma conditions:</p>
<ul>
<li>Pro forma 215 <em>Company auditor registration conditions</em> (<a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/pro-formas#pf215" title="Pro formas" data-anchor="#pf215">PF 215</a>)</li>
<li>Pro forma 216 <em>Authorised audit company registration conditions</em> (<a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/pro-formas#pf216" title="Pro formas" data-anchor="#pf216">PF 216</a>)</li>
<li>Pro forma 217 <em>Deed: authorised audit company run-off insurance cover</em> (<a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/pro-formas#pf217" title="Pro formas" data-anchor="#pf217">PF 217</a>)</li>
</ul>
<h3><a id="fees"></a>Fee payment</h3>
<p>Options for payment of fees can be found in the portal. For more information, see <a href="/for-business-and-companies/forms-and-fees/payment-options" title="Payment options">Payment options</a> or our Information Sheet 30:</p>
<p class="info-link">Information sheet 30 <em>Fees for commonly lodged documents</em> (<u><a href="/for-business-and-companies/forms-and-fees/all-fees/fees-for-commonly-lodged-documents" title="Fees for commonly lodged documents">INFO 30</a></u>).</p>
</div>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<h2>Lodging your application</h2>
<p><!-- START CALL OUT --></p>
<div class="asic-callout asic-callout--caution">
<div class="asic-callout__content">
<p>You must provide a complete application by <strong>submitting all required documentation simultaneously</strong> with the lodgement of the electronic application. We will return any application that is incomplete. You will then need to re-apply after you have rectified all deficiencies.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>See <a href="#tips" data-anchor="#tips">Useful tips and application templates</a> below for relevant Word templates when applying for auditor registration. You must prepare these documents and all required supporting information <strong>prior to submitting the electronic application</strong>.</p>
<h3>Lodgement options</h3>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h4>Start or resume an application or registration</h4>
<p>See options below to commence or resume an application for registration as an auditor or authorised audit company:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/cgi-bin/Lodgement/903AV001/start/ApplicationLogin" class="asic-button asic-button--primary">Start an application</a> <a href="https://www.edge.asic.gov.au/003/raudportal/get/ApplicationResume" class="asic-button asic-button--primary">Resume an application</a></p>
<h4>Lodge online</h4>
<p>You can lodge your application online using ASIC’s auditor portal. See Form 903 for more information:</p>
<p class="form-link">Form 903 <em>Application for registration as an auditor</em> (<a href="/regulatory-resources/forms/forms-folder/903-application-for-registration-as-an-auditor" title="903 Application for registration as an auditor">Form 903)</a></p>
<p>For more information about the portal, see <a href="/online-services/asic-portals/auditor-portal-access" title="Auditor portal access">Auditor portal access</a>.</p>
<h4>Lodge by email</h4>
<p>Scan and send a copy of your signed application and all required supporting documents to <a href="mailto:Auditor.Registration@asic.gov.au">Auditor.Registration@asic.gov.au</a>.</p>
<p>Make sure you include the applicant's name in the title of the email. Ensure the size of each email does not exceed 10 MB. You may send multiple emails to meet size constraints.</p>
<h4>If you are unable to apply online</h4>
<p>If you cannot lodge online, you can complete and send a paper form:</p>
<p class="form-link">Form 903 <em>Application for registration as an auditor</em> (<a href="/regulatory-resources/forms/forms-folder/903-application-for-registration-as-an-auditor" title="903 Application for registration as an auditor">Form 903)</a></p>
<p class="action-box-content-item">Send your application, cheque for the payment fee (if not paid by Bpay) and required documents to:</p>
<p style="padding-left: 40px;" class="action-box-content-item">ASIC<br>Auditor Registration team<br>PO Box 4000<br>Gippsland Mail Centre Vic 3841</p>
</div>
<div class="asic-callout asic-callout--important">
<h3 class="asic-callout__title">Information for applicants registering as an authorised audit company</h3>
<div class="asic-callout__content">
<p>Applicants for registration as an authorised audit company <strong>must send signed copies</strong> of PF&nbsp;217 <em>Deed: authorised audit company run-off insurance cover </em>(<a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/pro-formas#217" title="Pro formas" data-anchor="#217">PF&nbsp;217</a>) from each director to:</p>
<p>ASIC<br>Auditor Registration team<br>PO Box 4000<br>Gippsland Mail Centre Vic 3841</p>
<p>Please make reference to having posted the completed Deeds within the email containing the other required supporting documents.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2>How we assess your application</h2>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h3>Registered company auditor</h3>
<p>You must demonstrate that you have appropriate qualifications and skills, are capable, and fit and proper for ASIC to register you as an auditor.</p>
<h4>Pathways for application for registration</h4>
<p>There are various <a href="/for-finance-professionals/company-auditors#pathways" title="Company auditors" data-anchor="#pathways">pathways</a> available to you for applying for registration, depending upon your individual circumstances. These pathways are set out in Regulatory Guide 180:</p>
<p class="rg-link">Regulatory Guide 180 <em>Auditor registration</em> <a href="/regulatory-resources/find-a-document/regulatory-guides/rg-180-auditor-registration" title="RG 180 Auditor registration">(RG 180)</a>.</p>
<h3>Authorised Audit Company</h3>
<p>To be eligible for registration as an authorised audit company, you must demonstrate that your company meets requirements covering ownership and control of the company, professional indemnity insurance, fit and proper directors and external administration.</p>
<h3>Application refusal</h3>
<p>We can only assess complete applications. A complete application is one that includes all the required information and supporting documents. We will return incomplete applications to you.</p>
<p>If you do not meet all the requirements of s1280 of the <em>Corporations Act 2001</em>, we may refuse to register you, after giving you the opportunity to attend a hearing. If your registration is refused, we will provide reasons for refusal.</p>
<h3>Application approval timeframe</h3>
<p>We aim to assess your application within 28 days from receipt of a complete application. The process may take longer than 28 days, depending upon the complexity of your application and whether we need to request additional information from you.</p>
<p>We may ask for additional information during the assessment of your application. You must provide this information within the timeframe requested, or we will assess your application on the information previously provided.</p>
<p>If you do not meet all requirements including the provision of additional information, we may refuse your application for registration.</p>
</div>
<h2><a id="tips"></a>Useful tips and application templates</h2>
<!-- ACCORDION START -->
<div class="accordion accordion-expand">
<h3>Useful tips</h3>
<ul>
<li>To avoid delay in assessing your application, provide complete information that addresses all the application requirements and ensure that you pay the required fee.</li>
<li>ASIC cannot register a person who is disqualified from managing a corporation and may refuse to register a person who is not resident in Australia.</li>
<li>Applications on the basis of practical experience must provide information using Documents A, B. C and D of Appendix 1 of RG 180. See application template documents below.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Application templates</h3>
<p>The following documents have been reproduced in Word from Appendix 1 of RG 180:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3913992/document-a-appendix-1-published-30-june-2016.docx">Document A: Practical auditing and other equivalent experience (DOCX 34 KB)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3913986/document-b-appendix-1-published-30-june-2016.docx">Document B: Supervisor declaration (DOCX 45 KB)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/e22a54z3/document-c-appendix-1-published-1-august-2024.docx" title="RG 180 Document C Appendix 1 Published 1 August 2024">Document C: Capability report (DOCX 26 KB)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3914010/document-d-appendix-1-published-30-june-2016.docx">Document D: Capability declaration (DOCX 27 KB)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://download.asic.gov.au/media/3914004/document-e-appendix-1-published-30-june-2016.docx">Document E: Auditor competencies logbook (2016 competency standard) (DOCX&nbsp;43 KB)</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
